 | api-2 | Fixed: `tracing_layer` turns off the layer's location, thread, inactivity and target attributes; the subscriber `setup_tracer` installs filters the layer to spans at `INFO` and above (span-only, so log lines don't become span events either) (P-721); staged `DIVERGENCES.md` replacement row; test `exports_info_spans_without_layer_attributes_debug_spans_or_log_lines` | this commit |
 | api-3 | Fixed: the global propagator is set only when `setup_tracer` builds the provider (the registration seam gets a `built` flag), rustdoc says so (P-722); test `registers_the_global_propagator_only_for_a_provider_it_builds` (the seam's flag; the process-global propagator itself is not touched by unit tests) | this commit |
 | api-10 | Fixed: `tracing-opentelemetry = { version = "0.34", default-features = false }`; `tracing-log` leaves `Cargo.lock`; `cargo check -p strands --all-features --tests` and the telemetry tests pass | this commit |
+| api-5 | Fixed: both setters are `#[builder(default, with = FromIterator::from_iter)]` (P-723); callers in `telemetry/tests.rs` and `tests/live_telemetry.rs` updated; test `tests/api_surface.rs::trace_and_baggage_attributes_take_plain_pairs` (does not compile without the fix) | this commit |
